1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,200
[THUNDER RUMBLING]

2
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:06,800
Mom, I swear to God,
if you touch my car again...

3
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:08,500
Relax, Danny. It's in one piece.

4
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:11,000
Barely. You took out
the mailbox on Elm Street.

5
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:13,400
That mailbox had it coming.

6
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,300
- Where's Grandpa?
- Asleep in front of the TV.

7
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:19,800
He's been watching the same
cooking show since 1987.

8
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:23,100
<i>Good evening. Tonight's top story:</i>

9
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:26,900
<i>a fire at the Riverside chemical plant
has forced 300 families from their homes.</i>

10
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:29,000
Turn that off. We need to talk.

11
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:32,400
I know about the money, Danny.

12
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:34,600
What money?

13
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:37,900
Don't play dumb with me.
Forty grand doesn't just walk off.

14
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:40,700
Okay, look, I was gonna tell you,

15
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:43,500
but I needed to figure out
how to pay it back first.

16
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:45,800
Pay who back? Who did you borrow from?

17
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:47,900
Ray Kowalski.

18
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:50,500
(SIGHS) Oh, you idiot.

19
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:53,400
That man would sell his own mother
for a parking spot.

20
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:55,800
I know, I know. I screwed up, okay?

21
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:58,900
Screwed up? You're in way over your head.

22
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:02,100
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

23
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:04,300
Expecting someone?

24
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:05,600
No.

25
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:09,700
Evening, Mrs. Doyle.
Sorry to barge in like this.

26
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:12,300
Detective Harris.
It's been a while.

27
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:15,600
Not long enough, if you ask me.
Mind if I come in?

28
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:17,800
Do you have a warrant?

29
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:20,400
I'm not here to arrest anybody.
Yet.

30
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,800
Your son's name came up in a case
we're working. Ray Kowalski's crew.

31
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:27,300
My son doesn't run with that crowd.

32
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:30,100
With all due respect, ma'am,
that's not what I'm hearing.

33
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:33,500
- Danny, go upstairs.
- Mom, I can handle this.

34
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:35,000
Upstairs. Now.

35
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:38,400
♪ Hold on, the night is long ♪

36
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:41,000
♪ And the road won't wait for me ♪

37
00:01:42,300 --> 00:01:45,900
Kid's got a good heart.
Lousy taste in friends, though.

38
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,800
Cut the crap, Harris.
What do you want?

39
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:52,700
Kowalski's going down, one way or another.
I'd hate for Danny to go down with him.

40
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:55,600
So help me help him.

41
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:59,200
If this is some kind of trick...

42
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:01,900
No tricks. You have my word.

43
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,500
Your word isn't worth much
in this house, Detective.

44
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:07,800
Fair enough. Then think about Danny.
Sleep on it.

45
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:10,300
I'll swing by tomorrow at 9:00.

46
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:13,800
Hey, Mrs. Doyle? Break a leg
at the recital Sunday.

47
00:02:13,900 --> 00:02:16,200
How do you know about the recital?

48
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:18,000
It's my job to know things.

49
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:21,100
[DOOR CLOSES]

50
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:25,600
Grandpa? How long have you
been standing there?

51
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:28,900
Long enough to know
we're in deep trouble, kiddo.
